## On-demand, md5-verified data downloaded for 'long' tests, plus the per-worktree
## markers recording that a dataset was fetched. See tests/test_data_manifest.tsv
## and tests/fetch_test_data.sh. Both patterns are needed explicitly:
## 'tests/*/data' above is the wrong depth, and while the repo-wide '*.gz' would
## incidentally hide the FASTQ files it would not hide the .md5ok sidecars.
## No trailing slash: that form matches a directory only, and the cache is routinely a SYMLINK to
## one shared between worktrees (which is what keeps the committed goldens repo-relative, where
## BRESEQ_TEST_DATA_DIR would bake in an absolute path). With the slash the symlink showed up as an
## untracked file, one 'git add -A' away from being committed.
tests/data/downloads
tests/.test_data_stamps/
tests/*-local*/
tests/data/*-local*/
# ...but keep checked-in expected outputs even when they end in an otherwise-ignored
# extension (e.g. *.txt, *.tab above); runtime output* files stay ignored.
# Note tests/bam2cov/expected.tab predates the *.tab rule and is tracked already, so it
# is unaffected either way -- the negation is what lets a NEW .tab golden be committed.
!tests/*/expected*.txt
!tests/*/expected*.tab

src/breseq/breseq/
src/breseq/breseq
src/breseq/gdtools

